Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: tegra30: surface-rt: set up the digital microphone (WM8962 GPIOs and routing)

The Surface RT has a digital (PDM) stereo microphone behind the WM8962, wired
to two of the codec's GPIO pins as clock and data. Two things in the
devicetree kept it from ever working:

1. wm8962_probe() reads the codec's GPIO function registers and, unless one is
   set to DMICCLK and one to DMICDAT, disables the "DMICDAT" DAPM pin for good.
   Nothing configured them. Add the gpio-cfg property. Which pins carry the
   signals is not documented anywhere found, so this uses GPIO2 as DMICCLK and
   GPIO4 as DMICDAT, the example in the binding and the Wolfson reference
   design. On the device the registers then read 0x0013 and 0x8014.

2. The sound card is fully_routed, and on a fully routed card the codec's input
   pins are never a signal source: audio can only enter through a board-level
   microphone widget that is routed to the pin. The card has a "Digital Mic"
   widget (from tegra_asoc_machine.c) but nothing routed it to the codec, so no
   capture path could ever be powered: the ADCs, the input mux and the pin all
   stay off and recordings are all zeros in every input mode. Route "Digital
   Mic" to DMICDAT.

Whether GPIO2 and GPIO4 are the right pair is not known yet; the route alone is
the part that was shown to be missing (DAPM dump on the device).

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts	2026-10-31 20:54:27.048119210 +0100
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts	2026-11-01 02:57:35.745324612 +0100
@@ -321,6 +321,24 @@
 			PLLVDD-supply = <&vdd_1v8_vio>;
 			SPKVDD1-supply = <&vdd_1v8_vio>;
 			SPKVDD2-supply = <&vdd_1v8_vio>;
+
+			/*
+			 * The on-board digital microphone is wired to two of the
+			 * codec's GPIO pins as clock and data. Which pins is not
+			 * known (no schematic): GPIO2 as DMICCLK and GPIO4 as
+			 * DMICDAT is the guess from the binding's example and the
+			 * Wolfson reference design. The codec driver only enables
+			 * its digital microphone input when it finds these two
+			 * functions configured at probe.
+			 */
+			gpio-cfg = <
+				0x0000 /* 0: not a GPIO */
+				0x0000 /* 1: default */
+				0x0013 /* 2: DMICCLK */
+				0x0000 /* 3: no register */
+				0x8014 /* 4: DMICDAT (input) */
+				0x0000 /* 5: default */
+			>;
 		};
 
 		/* Texas Instruments TPS659110 PMIC */
@@ -901,7 +919,8 @@
 			"Headphone Jack", "HPOUTR",
 			"Headphone Jack", "HPOUTL",
 			"Int Spk", "SPKOUTR",
-			"Int Spk", "SPKOUTL";
+			"Int Spk", "SPKOUTL",
+			"DMICDAT", "Digital Mic";
 
 		nvidia,i2s-controller = <&tegra_i2s1>;
 		nvidia,audio-codec = <&wm8962>;
